      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND AND OBJECTIVES",
          "content": "Superior hypogastric plexus block has been used to treat cancer pain of the pelvis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "A patient with severe chronic nonmalignant penile pain after transurethral resection of the prostate underwent a single superior hypogastric plexus block with local anesthetic and steroid. The patient was also started on medications that treat neuropathic pain a few hours after the procedure was finished."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The superior hypogastric plexus block resulted in complete pain relief immediately after the procedure. The pain relief continued at 1, 2, 4, and 8 months follow up."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "In this case of severe penile pain the superior hypogastric plexus block was useful diagnostically and therapeutically."
        }
      ]},
